  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Olkaria Geothermal Power Total Flow Unit, through Langson Energy, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant is funding a feasibility study for the Kenya Electric Generating Company Limited (&quot;KenGen&quot;) that would support the implementation of a total flow topping unit to generate electricity from waste energy at KenGen&apos;s OW-733 geothermal well and assess the viability of deploying total flow topping units at other well sites in the Olkaria geothermal field in Kenya (&quot;Project&quot;). The feasibility study includes technical and financial analysis of the proposed Project and training. A U.S. company, Langson Energy, Inc. (Carson City, NV) is performing the feasibility study. A USTDA grant of $487,500 is funding a feasibility study for the Kenya Electric Generating Company Limited (&quot;KenGen&quot;) that would support the implementation of a total flow unit to generate electricity from underutilized energy at KenGen&apos;s OW-927A geothermal well and assess the viability of deploying total flow units at other well sites in the Olkaria geothermal field in Kenya (&quot;Project&quot;). The feasibility study includes technical and financial analysis of the Project and training for KenGen staff. A U.S. company, Langson Energy, Inc. (Carson City, NV) is performing the feasibility study.</narrative>
  </description>
